# Docker build context excludes.
#
# Without this file, `docker compose up --build` sends the ENTIRE repo
# (including multi-GB build caches that have nothing to do with the image)
# as build context on every build. Discovered 2026-09-16 while debugging a
# dev-sandbox build that filled the host disk and failed: rust/target/ alone
# was 53GB (accumulated Rust debug+release build artifacts across every
# crate), and node_modules/ (root + every sub-package) is reinstalled fresh
# inside the container by `RUN pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` in
# dev.Dockerfile anyway, so copying the host's copy in is pure waste (and
# would bake host-platform-specific native addon builds into a Linux
# container, which is actively wrong, not just slow).

# Rust build artifacts — never needed in the image; the dev sandbox mounts
# pre-built release binaries from the host (see docker-compose.dev.yml).
rust/target/

# Reinstalled fresh inside the container (dev.Dockerfile's pnpm install
# step) — copying the host's node_modules in is wasted transfer at best,
# and bakes in host-native-addon builds at worst.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Version control history — never needed inside the image.
.git/

# Editor/OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Local scratch files this session's debugging created — harmless but no
# reason to ship them into a build context either.
.diag_out.txt
.sandbox-build.log
